          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#4 · lines 33–40; the verified German closing words",
          "title": "Beginning and end joined; content and form",
          "italic": "The lyric demonstrates its own answer: the poem has carried blossom, valley, swimmer, changing eyes and the named wave into one formed sequence — the opening wish returns changed by the poem that answered it.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The final stanza gives another imperative: beginning and end are to draw together into one, faster than the objects themselves flee past the addressee. The opening asked that an early blessing stay for an hour; the ending asks for an act of gathering across passage. The Muses enter: their favour promises something imperishable, and thanks are asked. The closing lines distinguish what is carried in the breast from its form in the mind — Den Gehalt in deinem Busen / Und die Form in deinem Geist. The content borne inwardly and the form through which it is",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "apprehended have distinct places in the achieved whole. The promise remains the Muses': no sequel restores the earlier body or stops the valley's change; continuation is given through what the closing distinction makes available. The appointed relation is One in change, returning to the native Two Ones (human-amplified: yes): change reaches the perceiver, the body and the named identity; the concluding unity must receive those differences if it is to receive the poem at all. Equating poetic water with QL's 0 would add a symbol-key the appointment does not supply.\n\nOccurrences: the joined beginning and end (#0, #4); the Muses and thanks (#4); the breast/mind distinction (#4); the wave's element (#3, #4).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
